<%# locals: (layer: false) %>
<%# The pages of "Mein Konto", ONE list for the two places that show it:

    - the sidebar of an account page (common/_navigation_account, F44), where it is the
      sidebar's middle;
    - the account layer (common/_account_layer, Belegungstabelle F47), which rises over
      the sidebar of every other page when the reader clicks their name.

    Until 2026-11-12 the second place was a small menu of its own under the name,
    with four of these entries and none of the others (no billing accounts, no API
    tokens, no way to the other organisations): two lists of one area that did not
    agree. A new account page is one entry here and shows in both.

    layer: true adds what only the layer has: the cross that closes it (F20, at the
    end of the label row as F41 has it). The label has the form of the sidebar's other labels
    ("PROJEKTE", "VERWALTUNG"). %>
<div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 px-3 pb-1.5">
  <p class="section-label text-muted"><%= t('navigation.account_section') %></p>
  <% if layer %>
    <button type="button" class="inline-flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-md text-muted transition-colors hover:text-heading"
            title="<%= t('views.common.close') %>" aria-label="<%= t('views.common.close') %>"
            data-action="sidebar-layer#close">
      <i class="bi bi-x-lg text-xs" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    </button>
  <% end %>
</div>
<%# The rows come from NavigationHelper::ACCOUNT_PAGES (navigation plan D4): the same list
    names the pages, decides which row is marked (by the page's controller, never by typed
    paths) and tells the layout that a page is an account page. A new account page is one
    entry there. "Alle Organisationen" and "Gesamt-Inbox" are not here: the level above the
    organisations has its own sidebar (F48). Billing accounts are always listed: checking
    for an account would cost a role query per organisation on every page with the layer. %>
<ul class="flex flex-col gap-1" data-account-nav-list
    data-controller="return-referrer" data-action="turbo:before-fetch-request@document->return-referrer#refresh">
  <% account_pages.each do |page| %>
    <%= render 'common/navigation_item', name: page[:label], path: page[:path], icon: page[:icon],
                                         active: page[:active], aria_current: ('page' if page[:active]) %>
  <% end %>
</ul>
